asing order for the given\n                array by performing any number of right shift operations.\n                \n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_sorted(current_arr):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given array is sorted in non-decreasing order.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(current_arr) - 1):\n            if current_arr[i] > current_arr[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _perform_right_shift(current_arr):\n        \"\"\"Creates and returns a new array representing a single right shift operation.\"\"\"\n        if not current_arr:\n            return []\n        return [current_arr[-1]] + current_arr[:-1]\n\n    if not arr:\n        return True\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    current_arr = list(arr) # Create a mutable copy\n\n    # We need to check at most N different configurations (including the original)\n    for _ in range(n):\n        if _is_sorted(current_arr):\n            return True\n        current_arr = _perform_right_shift(current_arr)\n\n    return False", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/112": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/112", "solution": "def reverse_delete(s,c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Deletes characters from s present in c, then checks if the resulting string is a palindrome.\n    Returns a tuple containing the modified string and its palindrome status.\n    \"\"\"\n    def remove_characters(source_s, chars_to_remove):\n        \"\"\"Removes all characters from source_s that are present in chars_to_remove.\"\"\"\n        chars_set = set(chars_to_remove)\n        result_chars = []\n        for char in source_s:\n            if char not in chars_set:\n                result_chars.append(char)\n        return \"\".join(result_chars)\n\n    def is_palindrome(text):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given string is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        return text == text[::-1]\n\n    # Step 1: Remove characters\n    resulting_string = remove_characters(s, c)\n\n    # Step 2: Check if 